Package: SurvX
Type: Package
Title: Survival, Competing Risks and Cure Regression Models
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Habib", "Ezzatabadipour", email = "habibezati@outlook.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Robert", "Gray", role = "cph",
           comment = "variance computation of the K-sample test, ported from the Fortran routine crstm of package cmprsk"))
Description: Estimators, tests and regression models for time-to-event data with one event
    type or with competing risks, computed in a dependency-free C++ core with an 'S7' interface.
    Kaplan-Meier and Aalen-Johansen estimators, log-rank and Gray tests, restricted mean survival
    time and the Nelson-Aalen and kernel-smoothed hazard; Cox regression (Cox 1972
    <doi:10.1111/j.2517-6161.1972.tb00899.x>) with strata, delayed entry, time-varying covariates
    and coefficients, case weights and robust variance; cause-specific hazards and Fine-Gray
    regression (Fine and Gray 1999 <doi:10.1080/01621459.1999.10474144>), with delayed entry;
    parametric survival regression (exponential, Weibull, Gompertz, log-normal, log-logistic,
    generalized gamma, piecewise exponential and Royston-Parmar spline, as proportional hazards or
    accelerated failure time models); mixture and non-mixture cure models; and the direct
    parametric models for the cumulative incidence function of Jeong and Fine (2006)
    <doi:10.1111/j.1467-9876.2006.00532.x> and Jeong and Fine (2007)
    <doi:10.1093/biostatistics/kxj040>. Also residuals, proportional hazards tests, prediction,
    prediction performance (Brier score, time-dependent AUC, calibration) and cross-validated
    model comparison. Every result names the publications it rests on, and the results were
    checked against established reference implementations.
